{"meta":{"dataset":"consumer-sentinel","title":"FTC Consumer Sentinel reports by state: fraud, identity theft and imposter scams, 2024 Data Book","version":"1.0.0","doi":"10.5281/zenodo.23741876","doiUrl":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23741876","conceptDoi":"10.5281/zenodo.23741875","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","attribution":"Source: Probative, FTC Consumer Sentinel reports by state: fraud, identity theft and imposter scams, 2024 Data Book, version 1.0.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23741876, licensed CC BY 4.0.","citation":"Probative. (2026). FTC Consumer Sentinel reports by state: fraud, identity theft and imposter scams, 2024 Data Book (Version 1.0.0) [Data set]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23741876","disclaimer":"Not legal advice. These are counts of reports made to the FTC, kept for marketing planning. A report is a consumer's account, not a finding that fraud happened, and the state tables leave out reports from state-specific data contributors. Deadlines and rights are for your own counsel.","notice":"Probative is a marketing firm, not a law firm; not legal advice.","lastChecked":"2026-10-27","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/consumer-sentinel/index.json","humanUrl":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/consumer-sentinel/","statusCodes":{"P":"primary source","S":"secondary source","D":"ABA model default","U":"open question"}},"summary":"Reports that consumers made to the U.S. Federal Trade Commission's Consumer Sentinel Network in 2024, by state, DC and Puerto Rico, from the FTC's Consumer Sentinel Network Data Book 2024. Four records per jurisdiction: fraud and other reports and identity theft reports (each with the count, the rate per 100,000 people and the FTC's rank among the 50 states), imposter-scam reports (the share of the state's reports that the FTC prints, with a count and a rate derived from it, flagged as rounded) and fraud reports with the share reporting a loss, the total